---The ScreenConvert table contains functions which will convert to and from screen positions and in-game coordinate
---positions.
---
---Info: Conversions from a screen position into a CoordGrid or CoordFine without supplying a `level` will output at the
---same level as the active player character.
---@class ScreenConvert
ScreenConvert = {}

---Returns the CoordGrid under the given screen position. Resulting coord will be on the same `level` as the player
---character.
---@param position Vector2 The XY screen position to convert.
---@return CoordGrid? # The tile coordinate to return. Returns `nil` if the active player or game world is unavailable, or if there is no tile beneath the given screen position.
---@overload fun(position: Vector2, level: integer): CoordGrid?
---@overload fun(x: integer, y: integer): CoordGrid?
---@overload fun(x: integer, y: integer, level: integer): CoordGrid?
function ScreenConvert.ScreenToCoordGrid(position) end

---Returns the CoordFine under the given screen position. Resulting coord will be on the same `level` as the player
---character.
---@param position Vector2 The XY screen position to convert.
---@return CoordFine? # The tile coordinate to return. Returns `nil` if the active player or game world is unavailable, or if there is no tile beneath the given screen position.
---@overload fun(position: Vector2, level: integer): CoordFine?
---@overload fun(x: integer, y: integer): CoordFine?
---@overload fun(x: integer, y: integer, level: integer): CoordFine?
function ScreenConvert.ScreenToCoordFine(position) end

---Returns the screen XY position, as a Vector2, of the given CoordGrid. The position is calculated from the centre of
---the coordinate tile. An optional in-game vertical offset `heightAboveGround`, which in Fine units, can be applied to
---the coordinate.
---@param coordGrid CoordGrid The tile coordinate to convert to a screen position. Calculations are made from the centre of the tile.
---@param heightAboveGround integer An additional vertical offset, in Fine units, to add to the tile position before converting.
---@return Vector2? # The resulting screen XY position. Returns `nil` if the game world or ground data for the given coordinate is unavailable.
function ScreenConvert.CoordGridToScreen(coordGrid, heightAboveGround) end

---Returns the screen XY position, as a Vector2, of the given CoordFine. An optional in-game vertical offset
---`heightAboveGround`, which in Fine units, can be applied to the coordinate.
---
---Info: The vertical component of `CoordFine.position.y` is ignored. Only `CoordFine.position.x` and
---`CoordFine.position.z` are used to calculate the ground height at `CoordFine.level`. The value of `heightAboveGround`
---is then added to the ground height before converting. If you need to convert a position with an explicit vertical
---component, use ScreenConvert.Vector3ToScreen.
---@param coordFine CoordFine The tile coordinate to convert to a screen position. The vertical position component is ignored (see above).
---@param heightAboveGround integer An additional vertical offset, in Fine units, to add to the tile position before converting.
---@return Vector2? # The resulting screen XY position. Returns `nil` if the game world or ground data for the given coordinate is unavailable.
function ScreenConvert.CoordFineToScreen(coordFine, heightAboveGround) end

---Returns the screen XY position, as a Vector2, of the given Vector3, in Fine units.
---
---Info: This method does not perform a ground height look-up, and so will perform better than coordinate-to-screen
---conversions.
---@param vec3 Vector3 The world position, in Fine units, to convert to a screen position.
---@return Vector2? # The resulting screen XY position. Returns `nil` if the game world is unavailable.
function ScreenConvert.Vector3ToScreen(vec3) end
